{"metadata":{"role":"collection","externalID":"TrackerTesting","modules":[{"name":"TrackerTesting"}],"title":"TrackerTesting","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Recording a body’s events","anchor":"Recording-a-bodys-events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-8blfh","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-mlec","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-26pul","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-pnmv"]},{"title":"Reading what was tracked","anchor":"Reading-what-was-tracked","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a tracker, binds it to the current task with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length of its body, then finishes it and returns a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" of every event tracked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through it. Each call makes its own tracker, so tests that run at once never see each other’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events. Events tracked after the body returns, by work it started but didn’t wait for, are dropped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There are four spellings. The body can be synchronous or asynchronous, and it can take the tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a parameter, for code that is handed its tracker (a 